<.shell title="Filter form" current={:filter_form}>
  <h1>Filter form</h1>
  <p class="lead">The filters above a list.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.filter_form for={to_form(%{})} id="filter-form-demo" onsubmit="return false">
      <.input id="filter-form-q" name="q" label="Search" value="" />
      <.input
        id="filter-form-status"
        name="status"
        type="select"
        label="Status"
        options={[{"All", "all"}, {"Draft", "draft"}, {"Published", "published"}]}
        value="all"
      />
    </.filter_form>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    Above a table people narrow down: a search box and a few menus. Changing one updates the list straight away, so there is no button.
  </p>

  <h2>When not to use</h2>
  <p>
    A form that saves something. Use <a href={page_path(:forms)}>inputs</a> with a Save button.
  </p>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.filter_form for=&#123;@form&#125; id="…"&gt;</code>
    around <code>&lt;.input&gt;</code>s. It sends <code>change</code>
    on every edit and on Enter, so the LiveView handles one event. A plain form with only phx-change posts itself on Enter and gets a 404. The
    <a href={page_path(:filter_a_list)}>Filter a list</a>
    pattern shows it with a table.
  </p>
</.shell>
